==============================================================================
[OK]   kappa needed for Milgrom's a_0 = c H_Lam/(2 pi) is Z/(4 pi) = sqrt(2/(3 pi))
[OK]   w(kappa_Milgrom) = -1/2  ==>  kappa_M is NOT algebraic (Theorem 2), so the 2 pi form requires a TRANSCENDENTAL knob  | kappa_M = 0.460658865962
[OK]   gap Z vs 2 pi reproduces the corpus's 8.20% (mean-relative) to 0.05 pts  | mean-relative gap = 8.1904% ; a_0 ratio 2pi/Z = 1.085402 (i.e. +8.54% in a_0)
[OK]   the two coefficients sit in DIFFERENT weight classes (-1/2 vs -1), so their ratio is not algebraic and no rational kappa closes the gap
       TENSION, on the record and against interest: THEORY favours 2 pi (EVEN,
       Milgrom's own coefficient) while DATA favours kappa = 1/2 (~2.2 sigma,
       QUOTED from project_kappa_discriminability, not re-derived here).  If the
       2 pi reading is right, the framework's knob is transcendental and the
       'one rational parameter' economy claim is lost.

