==============================================================================
[OK]   E3 is REAL: Wallis partial products are exactly RATIONAL at every order  | e.g. N=10 -> 68719476736/44801898141
[OK]   E3 is REAL: those rationals converge to pi/2, error strictly decreasing, |W_2000 - pi/2| < 1e-3  | errors: N=10:3.69e-02, N=100:3.90e-03, N=1000:3.92e-04, N=2000:1.96e-04
[OK]   E3 is REAL: no partial product EQUALS pi/2 (rational vs transcendental)
       ==> a mode sum, infinite product or functional determinant CAN produce
       pi, and with an odd-dimensional measure a HALF power of it, out of
       algebraic input.  The corpus phrase 'structurally gauge-blind' must be
       read as 'no finite algebraic identity', not 'no derivation'.

